  "question": {
    "text": "Let the $x-z$ plane be the boundary between two transparent media. Medium 1 in $z \\geq 0$ has a refractive index of $\\sqrt{2}$ and medium 2 with $z < 0$ has a refractive index of $\\sqrt{3}$. A ray of light in medium 1 given by the vector $\\vec{A}=6 \\sqrt{3} \\hat{i}+8 \\sqrt{3} \\hat{j}-10 \\hat{k}$ is incident on the plane of separation. The angle of refraction in medium 2 is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "T2njk",
      "text": "\n$45^{\\circ}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "AmCbx",
      "text": "\n$60^{\\circ}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SQJDg",
      "text": "\n$75^{\\circ}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "mdK0y",
      "text": "\n$30^{\\circ}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Normal to the plane is $z$-axis\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\cos \\theta_1=\\frac{A_z}{A}=\\frac{10}{20}=\\frac{1}{2}, \\theta_1=60 \\\\\n& \\mu_1 \\sin \\theta_1=\\mu_2 \\sin \\theta_2 \\Rightarrow \\sqrt{2} \\times \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}=\\sqrt{3} \\sin \\theta_2 \\Rightarrow \\theta_2=45^{\\circ}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
